{
  "name": "1941_heraklion",
  "title": "Battle of Heraklion, May 1941 (Operation Mercury)",
  "notes": "Battle of Crete / Operation Mercury, 20-29 May 1941. Researched (Davin 'Crete' NZ Official History App. IV strengths, Playfair 'Med & ME' Vol II ch. VII, en/el Wikipedia Battle of Heraklion + Battle of Crete OOB, Beevor/MacDonald). AXIS: Kampfgruppe Brauer's paratroopers dropped ON the town/airfield 20.5, but the decisive German concentration after the failed first day lay WEST of the town — III./FJR 1 dug in SW of it and II./FJR 2 threw a block astride the Rethymno coast road ~2 miles west, and every follow-up attack (21-27.5) came at the town gates from the W/SW; the airlanded 5. Geb.Div. went to Maleme and the seaborne Heraklion force never landed. dirs=W (hills province 1164) mirrors that axis. ATTACKER (9 bns, ~4,200 men modeled): Kampfgruppe Brauer = FJR 1 (I./Walther east/Ames Ridge, II./Burckhardt airfield, III./Schulz SW of town, all org 55) + II./FJR 2 (2 companies, west-flank screen/road block, org 40) + 1 co Fsch-MG-Btl.7 (org 35) + Fsch-Art.-Abt. 7 det (7.5cm GebG 36 air-dropped, towed) + Fsch-Pz.Jg-Abt. 7 det (3.7cm PaK 36, piercing 45) + 24.5 parachute drop (4 companies W of town) + 27.5 Gournes drop (both org 40). DEFENDER (17 bns, ~7,000 men): 14th Inf Bde (Chappel) = 2/Black Watch (867, East Hill, sappers), 2/York & Lancaster (742), 2/Leicestershire (637, inner perimeter), 1/A&SH (340 of 655 arrived 25-27.5 from Tymbaki, org 45), 7 Med Rgt RA (320 men, GUNS NOT ON CRETE — fought as infantry, org 30), 234 Med Bty (13 captured 75/100mm guns, SE of airfield), Sec 15 Coast Rgt (2x4-inch), B Sqn 7 RTR (2 Matilda II, one at each runway end) + 3rd Hussars det (6 Mk VI); 2/4th Australian Inf Bn (553, 19 Aust Bde attached — 'the Charlies' hills over the airfield) + 10 Bofors (7 Aust LAA + 156 LAA Tp) + C Hvy AA Bty RM (4x3-inch); Greeks = 3rd Gr Regt (2 bns, org 40), 7th Gr Regt (1 bn, org 40), Garrison Bn (5. Div. left behind, org 40), Cretan Gendarmerie (org 30). EXCLUDED (never fought at Heraklion): the 2nd Motor Sailing Flotilla (~4,000 men = II./GJR 85 + most of the div. artillery/AA) turned back by Force C off Milos 22.5; I./II./GJR 100 airlanded at MALEME (none reached Heraklion); the Luftlande-Sturm-Regiment fought at Maleme/Chania; the ~2,000-man parachute drop of 28.5 landed east of the perimeter and saw no engagement before the night 28/29 evacuation; ~600 paras of the group never left the Greek airfields. NO German armor (none existed on Crete); no defender AT company (none documented in the sector). HISTORICAL OUTCOME: the garrison held — the airborne assault was bloodily repulsed and the town fell only after the night 28/29 evacuation (defender-favored, like Ioannina). NO player_side field: the script does not prescribe who the player commands — default attacker (the historical aggressor), flip freely in the menu/CLI; enemy_tactic=elastic_defense is the AI card for the default enemy (the garrison), headless runs set both cards explicitly. Division compositions follow the P2 ruling: NO pure-artillery divisions — every gun/AA/AT unit rides a line division, and 7 Med Rgt is infantry (it had no guns). Stats = 1939 calibration (only 1940-era tanks present).",
